# Privacy Policy for Pit Wall Duel

Effective date: 11 October 2026

This policy describes how Pit Wall Duel handles information on iPhone and iPad.

## 1. Overview

Pit Wall Duel is an offline game about identifying racing circuits and locating them on a world map. You can play against another person on the same device or against a local bot.

There is no registration or account system. The app does not send player names, settings, answers, scores, or map guesses to the developer or to a game server.

The current version contains no advertising, third-party analytics, or tracking SDKs. Apple-operated services and information you voluntarily send when contacting support are described separately below.

## 2. Information Stored on Your Device

The app remembers the following information locally:

- Optional display names for the two players.
- Your opponent selection and bot difficulty.
- Race settings, including the circuit collection, number of rounds, circuit display mode, and rotation preference.
- Your selected language: English or Croatian.
- Your music, sound-effect, and haptic-feedback preferences.
- Whether you have completed or skipped the first-run walkthrough.

This information is used to personalise the interface, configure races, and remember your choices between launches. Player names can be nicknames or left blank; they are not verified identities or account credentials.

Preferences are stored using the app's local WebKit storage and iOS preferences storage. They are not published to other players or sent to the developer.

## 3. Gameplay, Maps, and Device Permissions

During a race, the app processes your answers, response times, map pins, scores, and round results in memory. These are used to run the race and show its results. The app does not maintain a permanent history of completed races.

Map pins represent your guesses about a circuit's location. They are not readings of your device's location. The map and circuit coordinates are bundled with the app, and the app does not use GPS or request Location Services permission.

The current app does not request access to your camera, microphone, photo library, contacts, or health data. Playing music and sound effects does not involve recording audio.

## 4. Offline Operation and the Bot

Game content, maps, translations, music, and sound generation are included with the app. Gameplay does not require requests to external websites or servers.

The bot runs entirely on your device using local difficulty rules. Your gameplay is not sent to an AI provider, and the app does not use a remote language model.

There is no Game Center integration, online matchmaking, chat, or developer-operated cloud synchronisation. Two-player mode shares the same physical screen, so another person using that device can see the displayed names and game information.

## 5. Children and Player Names

The same offline data handling applies regardless of a player's age. The app does not ask players to provide their age, contact information, or a real name, and it does not transmit their gameplay information to the developer.

Parents and guardians can leave player names blank or use nicknames. Avoid entering sensitive information in a name field, particularly on a shared device.

## 6. Device Storage and Backups

Saved preferences remain in the app's local storage. The app does not create a developer-managed cloud copy or synchronise them with another device.

Depending on your device and Apple settings, app data may be included in iCloud or computer-based device backups. Those backups are managed outside Pit Wall Duel and are not accessible to the developer through the app.

You can manage backup inclusion and existing backups using Apple's settings and tools. See [Apple's guidance on managing iCloud storage](https://support.apple.com/en-us/108922).

## 7. Retention and Deletion

Saved names and preferences remain on the device until you change them or remove the app and its data. You can edit or clear either player-name field in the race setup. A blank field uses a default player label.

Race answers, scores, and map guesses are not written to a persistent match-history database. Leaving a race, starting a new race, or terminating or reloading the game session discards the previous session's results from the app.

There is no reset-all or data-export control in the current version. To remove the app's saved local data, choose **Delete App** in iOS or iPadOS. **Offload App** retains documents and data for later reinstallation. See [Apple's explanation of app storage and removal](https://support.apple.com/en-la/108429).

Deleting the app does not automatically remove copies that may already exist in device backups. Manage those backups separately; restoring a backup may restore saved app preferences.

The developer cannot remotely read, recover, or delete the game data stored on your device.

## 8. Advertising, Analytics, and Tracking

Pit Wall Duel does not integrate advertising networks, third-party analytics, tracking pixels, or developer-operated telemetry. It does not use an advertising identifier or track activity across other apps and websites.

The developer does not receive local player names or gameplay records through the app and does not sell those records or use them for targeted advertising.

Apple may process App Store transactions, downloads, device diagnostics, and usage information under its own policies. Depending on your settings, Apple may provide developers with crash reports or aggregated app statistics. This is separate from the app's own storage and is governed by Apple's controls.

You can manage diagnostic sharing in **Settings > Privacy & Security > Analytics & Improvements**. See [Apple's App Analytics & Privacy information](https://www.apple.com/uk/legal/privacy/data/en/app-analytics/) and [App Store & Privacy information](https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/data/en/appstore/).

## 9. Security

The app relies on the application sandbox and security protections provided by iOS and iPadOS. It does not provide an additional in-app password or biometric lock for saved player names or settings.

Anyone with access to your unlocked device may be able to open the app and view that information. Use a device passcode, keep the operating system updated, and avoid putting sensitive information in player-name fields.

No device or storage system can be guaranteed completely secure.

## 10. Your Choices

You can:

- Play without entering a name or creating an account.
- Change or clear saved player names.
- Choose the language and race settings.
- Enable or disable music, sound effects, and haptics independently.
- Manage Apple's diagnostic-sharing and backup settings.
- Delete the app and its local data.
- Contact the developer with questions about this policy or applicable privacy rights.

If you choose to email the developer, your email address and anything you include in the message are received through the email service. That correspondence is used to respond to your request and handle related follow-up; it is separate from the app's on-device gameplay data. Please do not send sensitive information that is unnecessary for your question.

## 11. Changes to This Policy

This policy may be revised if the app's functionality or information handling changes. The effective date at the top will identify the updated version.

Any future feature that changes how information is collected or shared will be reflected in this policy, with additional notice or consent where required.

